.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dotman-init 1  "init "
.SH NAME
dotman\-init \- Create the dotman repo or set its remote, or clone a repo and apply it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotman init\fR [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-import\fR] [\fB\-\-keep\-local\fR] [\fB\-\-take\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-approve\-hooks\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-bootstrap\fR] [\fB\-\-refresh\-bootstrap\fR] [\fB\-\-git\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-git\-email\fR] [\fB\-\-git\-global\fR] [\fB\-\-create\-github\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-system\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-create\-key\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-key\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-age\-key\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIURL_OR_PATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create the dotman repo or set its remote, or clone a repo and apply it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be created and change nothing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SOURCE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-import\fR
Create a fresh repo without looking for an existing setup to import
.TP
[\fIURL_OR_PATH\fR]
Git URL or local path of an existing dotman repo to clone and apply
.SH REMOTE
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<URL>\fR
Set or replace the `origin` remote
.TP
\fB\-\-create\-github\fR \fI<OWNER/NAME>\fR
Create the private GitHub repo `OWNER/NAME` with `gh` and make it `origin`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-remote\fR
Do not ask for a remote
.SH DECISIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-local\fR
Keep the local version of files that differ from the repo
.TP
\fB\-\-take\-repo\fR
Take the repo version of files that differ, after backing them up
.TP
\fB\-\-approve\-hooks\fR
Approve the `[hooks]` table of the cloned repo on this machine and run its hooks
.SH "THIS MACHINE"
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-bootstrap\fR
Do not write install.sh, the script that sets up `dotman` in a container
.TP
\fB\-\-refresh\-bootstrap\fR
Rewrite install.sh with this version\*(Aqs script, unless it was edited
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Git `user.name` to set when git has no identity
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-email\fR \fI<EMAIL>\fR
Git `user.email` to set when git has no identity
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-global\fR
Store \-\-git\-name and \-\-git\-email in the global git config instead of the repo\*(Aqs
.TP
\fB\-\-host\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Host name of this machine, written to `[identity]` in the machine config
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
A profile this machine opts into, written to the machine config; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-system\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
A directory outside $HOME whose files this machine manages, added to `[system] roots`; repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-system\fR
Do not ask about system files
.TP
\fB\-\-create\-key\fR
Create an age identity for encrypted files
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-key\fR
Do not ask about an age identity
.TP
\fB\-\-age\-key\-file\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Import the age identity in FILE before applying, so encrypted files decrypt
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
With \-\-age\-key\-file: replace a different existing identity, after backing it up
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show verbose output
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational messages
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-pager\fR
Disable pager output
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-root\fR
Allow running as root
